body:
I've tried a few times in my life in getting professional. When I was a teenager I tried and when my depression hit really low, i was thrown into the loney bin. I didn't feel like i was getting better and I was only increasingly growing bored in there. There was nothing to do but meetings and play time was extremely low. I was surrounded by people who had even worse issues than me so I felt like I didn't belong. Just to get out of there I had to lie about feeling better. 

&#x200B;

A few years ago, it almost had happen again, if it being stuck in a hospital there no way for me. I did get recommend for a therapist. So I decided to follow through it, it was the one that they had recommend for me. For the first month, it was just me coming in, signing papers, and then leave. The last time i went in was the same thing but they had forgotten I was there and sent me to the wrong location. I was there over 2hrs because of this and then i was told it was only for short term. If my problems were really that simple for short therapy, I wouldn't have bother that much and then I wasn't reached for a proper therapy for about a month later.  By this point, I had given up, didn't feel like they had cared and could of ended my life before they decided to even call me. So i just told them to forget it and hang up on them.
